            {
                "citation_meta": [
                    {
                        "citation": "Article 7",
                        "description": "People who work in the processing of personal data, both in public and private organizations, are obliged to keep secret about them, when they come from or have been collected from sources not accessible to the public, as well as about others data and background information related to the data bank, an obligation that does not cease for having finished its activities in this field."
                    },
                    {
                        "citation": "Article 9",
                        "description": "Personal data must be used only for the purposes for which they were collected, unless they come from or have been collected from sources accessible to the public.\n    In any case, the information must be accurate, up-to-date and truthfully reflect the real situation of the data owner.\n    The making of all kinds of predictions or risk assessments is prohibitedthat are not based solely on objective information related to delinquencies or protests of the natural or legal persons of which it is reported. Violation of this prohibition will force the immediate elimination of said information by the person responsible for the database and will give rise to the corresponding compensation for damages."
