            "remediation": {
                "description": "<p>Ensure that your AWS S3 buckets are protecting their sensitive data at rest by enforcing Server-Side Encryption</p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Sign in to the AWS Management Console and open the Amazon S3 console at <a href=\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/s3/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://console.aws.amazon.com/s3/</a>.</li>\n\t<li>In the Buckets list, choose the name of the bucket that you want.</li>\n\t<li>Click the Properties tab.</li>\n\t<li>Under \"Default encryption\", choose Edit.</li>\n\t<li>Select Enable under \"Server-side encryption\" and click Save Changes.</li>\n\t<li>Repeat steps no. 2 – 5 for each S3 bucket available within your AWS account.</li>\n</ol>",
