            "description": "Ensure that Google Cloud Storage buckets are using lifecycle management rules to manage objects during their lifetime and help to save on Google Cloud Platform (GCP) storage costs. Lifecycle management rules apply actions to current and future objects when they meet user-defined conditions such as downgrading or deleting older objects, in order to help manage costs.\nNearline Storage class is best suited for *backups* and data accessed less than once a month. Coldline Storage is mostly used for *disaster recovery* and data accessed less than once a quarter.",
