            "remediation": {
                "description": "<p>The following steps describe how to set up logs delivery for a specific bucket using the <a href=\"https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/gsutil\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">gsutil tool</a>, the <a href=\"https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/xml-api/overview\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">XML API</a>, and the <a href=\"https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/json_api\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">JSON API</a>. </p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Create a bucket to store your logs using the following command:\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>gsutil mb gs://example-logs-bucket</pre>\n</div></div></li>\n\t<li>Assign Cloud Storage the <tt>roles/storage.legacyBucketWriter</tt> role for the bucket:\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>gsutil iam ch group:cloud-storage-analytics@google.com:legacyBucketWriter gs://example-logs-bucket</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>The role grants Cloud Storage, in the form of the alias <tt>cloud-storage-analytics@google.com</tt>, permission to create and store your logs as new objects.<br/>\nLog objects have the <a href=\"https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/access-control/lists#defaultobjects\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">default object acl</a> of the log bucket, unless <a href=\"https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/uniform-bucket-level-access\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">uniform bucket-level access</a> is enabled on the bucket.</p></li>\n\t<li>Enable logging for your bucket using the <tt>logging</tt> command:\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>gsutil logging set on -b gs://example-logs-bucket [-o log_object_prefix ] gs://example-bucket</pre>\n</div></div></li>\n</ol>",
