            "remediation": {
                "description": "<p>You can enable Autonomous Data Guard when Autonomous Database is available (Lifecycle State shows <b>Available</b>), as follows:</p>\n\n<p>Perform the following prerequisite steps as necessary:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Open the Oracle Cloud Infrastructure Console by clicking three horizontal lines next to Oracle Cloud.</li>\n\t<li>From the Oracle Cloud Infrastructure left navigation menu click <b>Oracle Database</b> and then, depending on your workload click one of Autonomous Data Warehouse, Autonomous JSON Database, or Autonomous Transaction Processing.</li>\n\t<li>On the Autonomous Databases page select your Autonomous Database from the links under the <b>Display Name</b> column.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>To enable Autonomous Data Guard do the following:</p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>On the <b>Autonomous Database Details</b> page, under Autonomous Data Guard, click <b>Enable</b> in the <b>Status</b> field.</li>\n\t<li>In the <b>Region</b> field, select a region.\n\t<ol>\n\t\t<li>To create a local standby database, select the Current Region. To create a cross-region standby database, select a different region.<br/>\nThe region list shows the current region for a local standby and remote regions where you can create a cross-region standby.</li>\n\t\t<li>If you select a different region, Autonomous Database shows the <b>Select a compartment</b> list. From this list, choose a compartment for the cross-region standby.</li>\n\t</ol>\n\t</li>\n\t<li>Click <b>Enable Autonomous Data Guard</b>.<br/>\nThe Autonomous Database Lifecycle State changes to <b>Updating</b>. In the <b>Resources</b> area with <b>Autonomous Data Guard</b> selected, the <b>State</b> field shows <b>Provisioning</b>. <br/>\nAfter some time, the <b>Lifecycle State</b> shows <b>Available</b> and the standby database provisioning continues.</li>\n</ol>",
