            "remediation": {
                "description": "<p>(1) Sign in to the AWS management console.<br/>\n(2) Navigate to the S3 dashboard at <a href=\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/s3/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://console.aws.amazon.com/s3/</a>.<br/>\n(3) Select the S3 bucket that you want to examine and click the Permissions tab.<br/>\n(4) In the Permissions tab, scroll down to the Access control list(ACL) and click edit at the right of the Access control list(ACL).<br/>\n(5) Search for Everyone (public access) and uncheck the Read option under the Bucket ACL column.<br/>\n(6) Click on save changes.</p>",
