            "remediation": {
                "description": "<p>The <b>default_retention_period</b> has been set to <b>24h (1 Day)</b>. Before the retention period, the object can not be deleted by the user.</p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Sign in to Google Cloud Management Console.</li>\n\t<li>Select the GCP project that you want to access from the console top navigation bar.</li>\n\t<li>Navigate to Google Cloud Storage dashboard at <a href=\"https://console.cloud.google.com/storage\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://console.cloud.google.com/storage</a>.</li>\n\t<li>In the navigation panel, select <b>Browser</b> to access all the buckets created for the selected GCP project.</li>\n\t<li>Click on the name of the storage bucket that you want to reconfigure (see Audit section part I to identify the right bucket), then select the <b>Bucket Lock</b> tab.</li>\n\t<li>On the <b>Bucket Lock panel, click on the edit policy button available next to the Duration</b> configuration attribute, to edit the retention policy defined for the selected storage bucket.</li>\n\t<li>Inside the <b>Edit retention policy configuration box, under Duration, set how long the objects within the selected bucket must be retained. Click SAVE CHANGES</b> to update the retention policy with the compliant retention period.</li>\n</ol>",
