            "remediation": {
                "description": "<p>1- Sign in to Google Cloud Management Console.</p>\n\n\n<p>2- Select the Google Cloud Platform (GCP) project that you want to access from the console top navigation bar.</p>\n\n<p>3- Navigate to Google Cloud BigQuery dashboard at <a href=\"https://console.cloud.google.com/bigquery\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://console.cloud.google.com/bigquery</a>.</p>\n\n<p>4- In the navigation panel, under Resources, click on the name of the dataset that you want to reconfigure. </p>\n\n<p>5- Click on the SHARE DATASET button from the dataset options menu to access the permissions defined for the selected BigQuery dataset.</p>\n\n<p>6- On the Dataset permissions panel, perform the following:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Select the DATASET PERMISSIONS tab to access the IAM permissions defined for the dataset.</li>\n\t<li>Click on the role associated with the allUsers and/or allAuthenticatedUsers member to expand the role configuration panel, and click on the delete (icon) button to remove the non-compliant IAM member.</li>\n\t<li>On the Remove member confirmation box, click REMOVE to confirm your action.</li>\n\t<li>Click Done to return to the selected BigQuery dataset dashboard.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>7- Repeat step no. 4 – 6 for each publicly accessible dataset created within the selected project.</p>\n\n<p>8- Repeat steps no. 2 – 7 for each project deployed in your Google Cloud account.</p>",
